 #### 24.2 Numeric representation and verification
 
 - Position is signed 64-bit encoder counts. Saturate on overflow and latch ARITHMETIC_RANGE; do not wrap commanded or accumulated physical position silently.
+- Approved local trajectory profile: position tolerance and the sum of maximum-speed braking distance plus one-tick lookahead must each be at most 2^28 encoder counts (268,435,456). Reject configurations outside this combined envelope; do not silently clamp them. Keep public positions and absolute/relative command fields 64-bit. Execute long commands through internal, frame-aligned local windows; update the frame offset at a coherent control-tick snapshot, including reverse motion. Internal frame/segment transitions must not stop the ramp, retire the command, restart its timeout, or change sequence/session identity. Completion requires the final target's existing position/velocity settling conditions. The current encoder capture counter remains 64-bit; rebasing applies to motion arithmetic, not resetting physical capture.
 - Public velocity and acceleration are signed milli-RPM and positive milli-RPM/second respectively. Duty uses signed int32 scaled by 65536 with magnitude bounded to one. Timestamps/durations are unsigned with explicit units.
 - Store encoder PPR, gearbox numerator/denominator, and calibration numerator/denominator as positive integers. Reject zero denominators. Cross-reduce rational factors before bounded multiplication. Preserve 468/10 and 10296/5 exactly for the default nominal profile.
 - Proposed initial software-visible range: encoder PPR 1..65,535; gearbox/calibration components 1..1,000,000; speed limit up to 1,000,000 milli-RPM; acceleration/deceleration up to 10,000,000 milli-RPM/s. Individual fields in range do not imply a valid combination: reject combinations exceeding capture rate, arithmetic width, or timing envelopes.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d90f770..ddbbbe4 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -110,3 +110,12 @@ five-clock HALT pipeline bound is 250 ns, within the 10 us budget.
 See `docs/verification.md` for profile-change validation. The reference Vivado
 design requires clock/reset integration changes; see `docs/vivado_reference.md`.
 RTL projects must compile `rtl/timing.sv` before `scheduler.sv` and `pwm.sv`.
+
+### Local position execution
+
+Long 64-bit position commands now use rebased 32-bit local trajectory coordinates.
+Internal frame transitions do not complete or restart the command. Position
+tolerance and maximum braking-plus-lookahead distance must each fit within
+268,435,456 encoder counts; invalid profiles fault during preparation. The hardware
+encoder count and public positions remain 64-bit. See `docs/motion_executor.md`.
+Rebasing currently increases measured resources; it is not a demonstrated LUT saving.
diff --git a/docs/motion_executor.md b/docs/motion_executor.md
index 1b585dc..95ed05d 100644
--- a/docs/motion_executor.md
+++ b/docs/motion_executor.md
@@ -238,3 +238,36 @@ boundaries and allocation directives live in the platform configurations. Sharin
 is local to each scheduled hierarchy; this is not a shared engine across motors.
 Prepared denominators are computed by the controller while disabled; the standalone
 motion top continues to prepare its own constants per call.
+
+
+## Rebased local trajectory coordinates
+
+`detail::RebasedPosition` maps each coherent 64-bit position snapshot to an
+aligned 2^28-count frame. `frame_ << local_position_bits` represents the absolute
+frame offset; the lower 28 position bits are the local coordinate. On command
+activation or frame change, the absolute target is converted to a local target.
+Targets in [-span, 2*span] relative to the frame origin are terminal targets;
+more distant targets use a bounded, nonterminal local target on the same side.
+The local signed error fits 32 bits, including overshoot and reversal. Rebasing
+uses the supplied snapshot directly, so no encoder edge is reset or discarded.
+Encoder capture and externally visible position remain signed 64-bit.
+
+Named constants are in `include/dmotor/detail/local_position.hpp`. Configuration
+preparation now rejects position tolerance above `local_position_span`, or
+`ceil(max_speed^2 * counts_num / braking_denominator) +
+ceil(max_speed * counts_num / lookahead_denominator)` above that span. Both are
+268,435,456 counts. This check preserves rational CPR and upward rounding; it is
+not a braking approximation. The combined controller prepares once while disabled;
+the standalone motion top still prepares on each call for its stateless config
+interface. Invalid profiles latch the existing configuration fault.
+
+A nonterminal target is always farther than the admitted braking/tolerance
+horizon from the real target. It therefore keeps the commanded direction/speed
+without braking at an internal boundary. Frame changes preserve the absolute
+target, ramp/integral, command identity, activation time and timeout. Only terminal
+coordinates can satisfy completion. Overshoot, immediate stop, authorization loss,
+faults and completion backpressure retain their previous behavior.
+
+This is local trajectory rebasing, not a 32-bit replacement for the hardware
+encoder accumulator. It adds rebase/preparation hardware and must not be claimed
+as a LUT saving; see the measured results in `verification.md`.
